---
import Landing from "../../layouts/Landing.astro";
---

<Landing
  title="AI game audio for Godot 4 · SEGAN"
  description="Let your AI agent make sound effects and music loops for your Godot 4 game: WAVs with loop points in their .import files, AudioStreamRandomizer and AudioStreamSynchronized resources. Free and open source."
  heading="AI game audio for Godot 4, as resources Godot loads"
  points={[
    "Loop points written into each WAV's <code>.import</code>: music loops by itself, sample-exact.",
    "An <b>AudioStreamRandomizer</b> <code>.tres</code> for every SFX with variations: play it, get a different one each time.",
    "An <b>AudioStreamSynchronized</b> <code>.tres</code> per song with stems: fade layers in and out for adaptive music.",
    "Sections, bars and markers in <code>manifest.json</code>, in samples and seconds, for syncing game events; <code>segan build --verify-godot</code> loads and plays everything in headless Godot.",
    "Free, MIT, offline. Your agent writes the sounds; you review them like code, and approve them by ear.",
  ]}
  code={`# segan.toml, next to your Godot project
output_dir = "../game/assets/generated/audio"
export = ["wav", "godot", "stems"]

# in GDScript
$Music.stream = load("res://assets/generated/audio/music/dungeon.wav")
$Music.play()      # loops on its own loop points
$Coin.stream = load("res://assets/generated/audio/sfx/coin.tres")
$Coin.play()       # a different variation each time`}
>
  <p>
    SEGAN is a text language for game audio. Your agent (Claude with the SEGAN skill, or any agent over
    MCP) writes the kits, sound effects and songs; <code>segan build</code> turns them into WAVs and Godot
    resources that drop straight into your project.
  </p>
</Landing>
